{"Title":"An Act relative to funeral directors","BillNumber":"H4475","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J17","Name":"Joint Committee on Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17","ResponseDate":"2024-01-25T08:44:31.383"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:13:22.76"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4475/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":null,"DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 83 of chapter 112 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting at the end thereof  the following new paragraph:- \r\n\t“All establishments and branches thereof for the preparation, disposition and care of dead human bodies shall participate in the program described in section 9 of chapter 117A as a condition for continued licensure.”   \r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect on December 31, 2024.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Redraft","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}